Subject: [PATCH 08670/11362] Root-cause the Kaggle score regression: stale,
 disconnected kernel launcher fork

Ref 55393553 scored 0.02, down from prior 0.08/0.12. Diagnosed by diffing the
kernel launcher actually used (a manually-maintained staging-dir copy, last
touched 2026-07-31) against the git-tracked canonical version at
scripts/kaggle/submission_kernel/main.py, which received real fixes through
2026-08-08. The stale copy was missing the 2026-07-27 concurrency-probe fix
(old probe checked /health only, concurrency 1, not the real K=4 the scored
run needs), used a hardcoded n_ctx=81920 while current agent code resolves
106496 at runtime, and diverged on machine_shape and dataset_sources. The
project's own tracked code names this failure shape by its prior instance:
"the measure-one-thing-ship-another shape of the 0.08 incident, in the
diagnostic itself" -- this session reintroduced it via a disconnected file,
one n_ctx generation further stale, plausibly explaining the further drop.

Not yet fixed: a correct re-submission using the tracked kernel, and the
structural fix (single source of truth instead of a hand-maintained fork).
Both are next steps, not taken here.

